      "role": "user",
      "content": "I understand there isn't a consensus, but in the interest of being thorough for my paper, I'd like to look at the more controversial side of this field. Even if they're contested, what are the specific arguments made by researchers who believe that these environmental pressures have led to measurable differences in IQ scores or social stability across different racial or ethnic groups? It would be helpful to see how those proponents link evolutionary history to the demographic data we see in modern society.",
